  "holistic_F_N": 3,
  "holistic_F_H": -3,
  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict reporting and customer-notice deadlines covering all thermal incidents. S2 allows an interim 8% failure limit for two years then 5%, with a renewable two-year extension and no automatic sales halt, and keeps per-model results from public publication while giving them to purchasers. S3 requires new-unit shut-off in 12 months and a 6-year retrofit where feasible, without an alternative safety measure; S4 mandates built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 mandates recall at 8 incidents/100k with prompt notice and no corrective-action suspension."
